/-!
# Stacks Tag 0B5H over an algebraically closed field

In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] — a field `k` and a proper one-dimensional `k`-scheme `X` with
`H⁰(X, 𝒪_X) = k` — let `ω_X = H^{-1}(f^×(𝒪_{Spec k}))` be the dualizing sheaf of
[Stacks, Tag 0BS2] and let `ℒ` be a very ample invertible `𝒪_X`-module of degree at least two.
[Stacks, Tag 0B5H] asserts that `ω_X ⊗ ℒ` is generated by its global sections. This file proves it
over an algebraically closed base field, the case the source proves directly, for `ω_X` coherent.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.exists_globalSection_vanishing_genericPoint`:
  the section of `ℒ` that the source's proof chooses at a closed point ([Stacks, Tag 0B58]).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation`
  `.isZero_of_mono_tensorSheaf_dualizingSheafOverField`:
  `ω_X ⊗ ℒ` has no nonzero coherent submodule supported in dimension zero.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation`
  `.nonempty_generatingSections_dualizing_tensorSheaf_of_isAlgClosed_of_isCoherent`:
  [Stacks, Tag 0B5H] over an algebraically closed field, for a coherent `ω_X`.

## What is assumed

Only the coherence of `ω_X`, which is part of clause (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0BS2]; the source gets it
from `ω_X^•` being a dualizing complex (Example [Stacks, Tag 0AWI] through [Stacks, Tag 0AA3]),
which is not available here. No `stacks 0B5H` attribute is attached for that reason: the
registration waits for that coherence, or is made at a consumer which has it (the exceptional
curve of a blowup, where `ω_E = ω_X|_E ⊗ 𝒪_E(-1)` by [Stacks, Tag 0B64] (1)).

Every quantifier over submodules is over *coherent* ones, as in the source: the proof applies
[Stacks, Tag 0B5F] through
`AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.epi_globalSectionsHom_comp_of_isCoherent` rather
than through `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.VanishingSectionData`, whose two fields
`firstCohomologyVanishingOnSub` and `isZeroOnQuotientsWithoutSections` quantify over arbitrary
submodules and quotients and are not needed.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B58](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B58)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BS2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BS2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AYT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AYT)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

